## Navigation 3 — Migration & New Projects

Navigation 3 is a ground-up rewrite designed exclusively for Compose, announced at Google I/O 2026. It replaces `NavHost`/`NavController` with `NavDisplay`/state-holder and removes the NavGraph concept entirely.

> **Use Nav 2.8+ (above rules) for existing projects unless migrating.** Use Nav 3 for greenfield projects or when ready for the migration.

### Install Nav 3

```toml
# gradle/libs.versions.toml
[versions]
navigation3 = "1.0.0-alpha01"   # check latest at d.android.com/jetpack/androidx/releases/navigation3

[libraries]
navigation3-compose  = { group = "androidx.navigation3", name = "navigation3-compose",  version.ref = "navigation3" }
navigation3-runtime  = { group = "androidx.navigation3", name = "navigation3-runtime",  version.ref = "navigation3" }
```

> Or install via Android CLI: `android skills add --skill=navigation-3`

### Key Concepts

| Nav 2 concept | Nav 3 equivalent |
|---|---|
| `NavController` | State holder (plain `mutableStateListOf<NavKey>`) |
| `NavHost` | `NavDisplay` |
| `composable { }` DSL inside `NavHost` | `entryProvider { addEntryProvider<Route> { } }` |
| `NavGraph` | Removed — use Kotlin scoping instead |
| `@Serializable` routes | `@Serializable` routes implementing `NavKey` |

### Routes — implement `NavKey`

```kotlin
import androidx.navigation3.runtime.NavKey
import kotlinx.serialization.Serializable

@Serializable
data object HomeRoute : NavKey

@Serializable
data class ProfileRoute(val userId: String) : NavKey

@Serializable
data object SettingsRoute : NavKey
```

### State Holder

```kotlin
// Replace NavController with a plain back stack list
val backStack = rememberSaveable { mutableStateListOf<NavKey>(HomeRoute) }

fun navigate(route: NavKey) { backStack.add(route) }
fun navigateBack() { if (backStack.size > 1) backStack.removeLast() }
fun popUpTo(route: NavKey, inclusive: Boolean = false) {
    val index = backStack.indexOfLast { it == route }
    if (index != -1) {
        backStack.subList(if (inclusive) index else index + 1, backStack.size).clear()
    }
}
```

### NavDisplay

```kotlin
NavDisplay(
    backStack = backStack,
    entryDecorators = listOf(
        rememberSaveableStateHolderNavEntryDecorator(),   // survives recomposition
        rememberViewModelStoreNavEntryDecorator(),         // scopes ViewModels to entries
    ),
    entryProvider = entryProvider {
        addEntryProvider<HomeRoute> { HomeScreen(onNavigateToProfile = { id -> navigate(ProfileRoute(id)) }) }
        addEntryProvider<ProfileRoute> { entry ->
            val route = entry.key  // type-safe, no string parsing
            ProfileScreen(userId = route.userId, onBack = ::navigateBack)
        }
        addEntryProvider<SettingsRoute> { SettingsScreen(onBack = ::navigateBack) }
    },
)
```

### ViewModel scoping with Nav 3

```kotlin
// ViewModel is scoped to the NavEntry — survives recomposition, cleared on pop
@Composable
fun ProfileScreen(
    userId: String,
    onBack: () -> Unit,
    modifier: Modifier = Modifier,
    viewModel: ProfileViewModel = viewModel(),   // scoped by rememberViewModelStoreNavEntryDecorator
) { ... }
```

### Migration from Nav 2 → Nav 3

1. Add Nav 3 dependency alongside Nav 2 (run in parallel during migration)
2. Convert routes: add `: NavKey` to existing `@Serializable` route classes
3. Replace `rememberNavController()` + `NavHost` with `mutableStateListOf<NavKey>` + `NavDisplay`
4. Replace `composable<Route> { }` blocks with `addEntryProvider<Route> { }` blocks
5. Replace `navController.navigate(Route)` call sites with `backStack.add(Route)`
6. Replace `navController.popBackStack()` with `backStack.removeLast()`
7. Remove `NavGraph` nesting — use `if`/`when` in `entryProvider` or extract Kotlin functions
8. Verify deep links still work — Nav 3 handles `Intent` deep links via `NavDisplay`'s `onBack` integration

### Nav 3 Checklist

- [ ] All routes implement `NavKey` and are `@Serializable`
- [ ] Back stack is `mutableStateListOf<NavKey>` wrapped in `rememberSaveable`
- [ ] `rememberSaveableStateHolderNavEntryDecorator()` included in `entryDecorators`
- [ ] `rememberViewModelStoreNavEntryDecorator()` included for ViewModel scoping
- [ ] No `NavController` references remain
- [ ] Deep links verified via `adb shell am start -d <uri>`

